quran[20]{c,v,t}:
  15,71,"He (Lut) said: ‘Here are my (people’s) daughters. If you desire to do something (then marry them, instead of committing indecency).’"
  15,72,"(O Prophet!) By your life, they wandered blindly in their (lustful) drunkenness."
  15,73,So the blast overtook them at sunrise.
  15,74,"Thus, We turned their town upside down and rained stones of baked clay upon them."
  15,75,There are indeed signs in that (destruction) for those who can anticipate.
  15,76,Indeed (the ruins of) these (destroyed towns) are still there on the highway.
  15,77,"Most surely, in this (account), there is a sign for the believers."
  15,78,"Indeed, the inhabitants of al-Ayka (the Woodland) were wrongdoers."
  15,79,"So We took vengeance upon them, and indeed (the ruins of) both (towns of Sodom and al-Ayka) are (visible) on an open highway."
  15,80,"Indeed, the inhabitants of al-Hijr (the Rocky Plain, also) denied the messengers."
  15,81,"And We had given them Our signs, but they turned away from them."
  15,82,"They used to carve out homes in the mountains, feeling secure."
  15,83,So the blast overtook them in the morning.
  15,84,And what they used to earn could not benefit them.
  15,85,"And We did not create the heavens, the earth and whatever is between them but with a true purpose. And the Hour is surely coming. So forbear with a graceful forbearance."
  15,86,"Indeed, your Lord is the All-Creator, the All-Knowing."
  15,87,"And indeed, We have given you the seven oft-repeated verses (i.e. Sura al-Fatiha) and the Glorious Qur’an."
  15,88,"Do not extend your glance towards (the worldly pleasures) that We have provided to some (disbelieving) groups of them, nor grieve for them. And lower your wing (of grace and affection) to the believers (to make them feel content)."
  15,89,"And (O Prophet!) say: ‘Indeed, I am the manifest warner,"
  15,90,"(carrying a warning) similar to what We sent to those who made divisions (in the Scriptures and the community),"
